    "An estimate of your VO₂ max, the maximum amount of oxygen your body can use during exercise. Apple Watch records one only after an outdoor walk, run, or hike on fairly flat ground with a good GPS and heart-rate signal, which is why most workouts show no value here." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "An estimate of your VO₂ max, the maximum amount of oxygen your body can use during exercise. Apple Watch records one only after an outdoor walk, run, or hike on fairly flat ground with a good GPS and heart-rate signal, which is why most workouts show no value here."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "对你的最大摄氧量（VO₂ max）的估算，也就是运动时身体能利用的最大氧气量。Apple Watch 只会在地势较平坦的户外步行、跑步或徒步后，且 GPS 与心率信号良好时记录一次，这就是大多数训练在这里没有数值的原因。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
